WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:06.609
"Dune," titled onscreen as "Dune: Part One,"
covers roughly the first half of Frank Herbert's

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:09.300
book, ending on something less than a cliffhanger.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:14.581
Until Part Two arrives, let's talk about where
"Dune" leaves off, and how we got there in

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.581
the first place.

00:00:16.581 --> 00:00:21.900
In a far-flung future deep in space, the planet
Arrakis is the center of an intergalactic

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.970
empire due to its natural resource "spice,"
a sought-after substance integral to interstellar

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:28.970
travel.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.480
When the film begins, that planet and its
spice mining industry is lorded over by House

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.410
Harkonnen and their sadistic head Baron Harkonnen.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:43.250
But the Emperor gives this prestigious station
to House Atreides, led by Duke Leto, leading

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.940
their entire family to move from their home
planet Caladan.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.740
But when they arrive on Arrakis, Leto discovers
that the entire operation has been internally

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.890
sabotaged.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:58.360
The Fremen, Arrakis' native inhabitants, still
seek to overthrow the imperial power structure

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.600
that oppresses them.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.150
The machinery necessary to mine spice effectively
all lies in various states of disrepair.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:10.890
And, of course, the Harkonnens left behind
an assassin entrenched in the palace walls

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.719
to make an attempt on the life of Leto's son
Paul.

00:01:13.719 --> 00:01:17.770
The only promising element of Leto's plans
for the new planet under his charge is in

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.299
his hopes to form an alliance with the Fremen.

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:21.899
But fate has other plans…

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:27.479
Baron Harkonnen, in collusion with the powerful
religious and political sisterhood known as

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:32.880
Bene Gesserit and the Emperor himself, hires
the Sardaukar, the Emperor's elite fighting

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.659
force, to attack House Atreides.

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:38.979
The Sardaukar attack under cover of night
with the Harkonnens' forces, led by Glossu

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:41.399
Rabban, bottlenecking them from the other
end.

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:45.590
The Baron also kidnaps the wife of Leto's
doctor Wellington Yueh in an effort to blackmail

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.459
him into helping with this coup.

00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:52.271
The Duke and Dr. Yueh are killed by the Baron,
and Dr. Yueh's last-ditch attempt to kill

00:01:52.271 --> 00:01:54.810
the Baron only leaves the latter wounded.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:59.920
But before this, Dr. Yueh also helps Leto's
son Paul and Paul's mother, Lady Jessica,

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.630
to escape the carnage, but they are captured
by the Harkonnens anyway.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.359
They are not, however, killed.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:10.060
As a complication from the Baron's alliance
with the Bene Gesserit, Jessica, part of the

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.489
sisterhood herself, and her son, who they
have plans for, are to be spared.

00:02:14.489 --> 00:02:17.760
But the Harkonnens hope to abandon them in
the middle of the desert, knowing there's

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.230
no way for them to reasonably survive its
harsh terrain.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:26.480
Lady Jessica and Paul are able to escape their
grasp, but still find themselves stranded

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.620
with only a pair of stillsuits to keep them
alive in the heat of Arrakis.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.890
As they struggle to find shelter for the night,
Jessica and Paul have to reckon with the visions

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.760
he has been seeing throughout the film.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.939
Paul has been secretly raised through his
training to be a mythical chosen one, a powerful

00:02:42.939 --> 00:02:45.710
being prophesied by the sisterhood's lore.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:47.510
As director Denis Villeneuve said,

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:51.069
"Everything around Paul's future is being
constructed by women."

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:56.970
He's basically, unwillingly, a years-long
eugenics experiment with nascent superpowers

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.150
destined to rule the universe one day.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:04.620
Meanwhile, in the present day, Paul and Jessica
reunite with Duncan Idaho, Paul's mentor and

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.180
friend, who has miraculously survived the
attacks.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:13.140
He helps them get away in search of a Fremen
sect to recoup and strategize with.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:17.560
Once there, they meet up with Dr. Liet-Kynes
the ecologist assigned by the Emperor to oversee

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.040
the regime change from Harkonnen to Atreides.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:25.390
Dr. Kynes knows that something pernicious
is afoot, but can't get more involved than

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.430
absolutely necessary, ultimately pledging
fealty to the Fremen and neither imperial

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:31.879
external force.

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:36.660
Paul has to accept that he is the head of
House Atreides now, and pledges to see through

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.549
his father's plans for the Fremen, thinking
he can work with them under the promise of

00:03:40.549 --> 00:03:42.409
freeing them from the empire.

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:44.099
But the Harkonnens have other plans…

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:50.250
The Harkonnens descend on this temporary hiding
place ready to finish the job on the Fremen

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:55.510
and the remaining Atreides survivors, but
Duncan Idaho locks Jessica, Paul and Dr. Kynes

00:03:55.510 --> 00:04:00.269
behind a stronghold door, intending to fend
off the wolves at the gate by himself to save

00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:01.269
them.

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:04.400
Throughout the film, Duncan has been his one
true friend.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.450
Now Paul must run away yet again, with his
mother and Dr. Kynes, as Duncan fights alone.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.319
"Duncan, can I trust you with something?"

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.370
"Of course, you know that."

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:20.739
Duncan goes "one vs. many" on the invading
hordes, taking out plenty of men before succumbing

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:22.009
to mortal wounds.

00:04:22.009 --> 00:04:27.530
With no remaining friendlies on Arrakis and
no other options, Paul and Jessica have to

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.850
soldier on in the desert hoping to find Fremen
who may or may not be sympathetic to their

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:33.850
cause.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:38.560
Jessica and Paul encounter Stilgar's sect
of Fremen, who initially see them as little

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.400
more than bodies of moisture to covet.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.560
Stilgar and Jamis are both in favor of just
killing them and taking the water from their

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:51.150
bodies, but Stilgar, remembering his meeting
with Leto, sees some merit in sparing Paul's

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.150
life.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.710
He just doesn't see that same merit in saving
Jessica's.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:01.060
Tensions rise to a boil when moves are made
to harm Jessica, who gets the upper hand on

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.250
Stilgar, leading to a standoff where Paul
finally meets Chani.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.380
She's the same woman he has been seeing in
his visions this entire time.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.740
But Jamis can't leave this infraction alone.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.690
By besting their leader in combat, Jamis has
to challenge Jessica to retain true control

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:22.000
over their sect, so he challenges her to fight,
with Paul having to step in as her champion.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.740
Paul's visions have seemingly been building
to this moment.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:30.050
Paul and Jamis fight, with Jamis clearly the
more ruthless combatant.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:34.990
At multiple points, Paul has Jamis dead to
rights, just like in the fencing style sparring

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.560
sessions he has with Gurney Halleck in the
film's first act, but this is no duel.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:44.080
The only way to win is to kill, which Paul
finally does.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:49.370
This marks Paul crossing over into his destiny,
finally abandoning his youth with all the

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.770
tragedies that have brought him to this moment.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:56.340
Jessica wants Stilgar to help them get off
world, but Paul sees that their future lies

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:57.340
here, with the Fremen.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:03.160
As Paul, Jessica, and the Fremen traverse
the desert on the way back to their stronghold,

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.889
he continues to be plagued by visions.

00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:11.080
He sees his eyes glowing blue, like Chani,
like the rest of the Fremen, and sees himself

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:15.150
leading a Fremen force in a war against the
rest of the Empire.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:18.259
"My road leads into the desert.

00:06:18.259 --> 00:06:20.699
I can see it."

00:06:20.699 --> 00:06:25.430
Whether we will actually see the other side
of this epic tale, of Paul's arc from boyhood

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:29.319
prodigy to reluctant messiah, remains to be
seen.

